# Booking version

The version lives in `package.json`, `CHANGELOG.md`, and a git tag `vX.Y.Z`. `v1.0.0` is the certificate purchase widget.

## On every commit

Bump the patch number before committing. `v1.0.0` becomes `v1.0.1`.

- Set `package.json` `version` to the new number.
- Add a `CHANGELOG.md` section for that version. Write it for the customer, in Russian, as bullet points: one visible change per line. No file names or implementation notes.
- Tag the commit `vX.Y.Z` and push the tag with the commit.

Do not bump the minor or major number for an ordinary commit.

## On a release build

When the user asks to build a release, bump the major number first. `v1.4.2` becomes `v2.0.0`. Reset minor and patch to 0.

- Update `package.json`, `CHANGELOG.md`, and the git tag the same way as a commit.
- Then run `pnpm build`.

```text
❌ commit stays on v1.0.0
✅ commit moves v1.0.0 → v1.0.1, changelog and tag included

❌ release build stays on v1.0.3 or only bumps the patch
✅ release build moves v1.0.3 → v2.0.0, then pnpm build
```
